$DATUM 2-([1,1'-Biphenyl]-4-carboxamido)-N,N,N-trimethylethan-1-aminium iodide.
Prepared according to the general procedure given in Table S2 in 0.2 mmol
scale. Yield 72.2 mg (88%) of white crystalline substance. M.p.
267.6-269.2 °C (dec.). Elemental analysis: For C18H23IN2O (410.30)
calculated (%):C, 52.69; H, 5.65; N, 6.86; found: C 52.66; H 5.76; N
6.79. 1H NMR (401 MHz, DMSO-d 6) O 8.89 (t, J = 5.6 Hz, 1H), 7.99 (d, J =
8.5 Hz, 2H), 7.85 (d, J = 8.5 Hz, 2H), 7.78 (d, J = 7.1 Hz, 2H), 7.54 (t,
J = 7.5 Hz, 2H), 7.46 (d, J = 14.6 Hz, 1H), 3.76 (q, J = 6.0 Hz, 2H),
3.57 (t, J = 6.5 Hz, 2H), 3.20 (s, 9H). 13C NMR (101 MHz, DMSO-d 6) O
167.21, 144.07, 139.92, 133.35, 129.98, 129.10, 128.79, 127.81, 127.59,
64.75, 53.51, 34.72.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM palladium embedded in cross-linked polyhydromethylsiloxane gel prepared
and used as catalyst, optimization study, optimized on catalyst,
Suzuki-Miyaura cross-coupling reaction
