$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 2-Allylbenzaldehyde PdCl2(PPh3)2 (2.5 mol%) and aqueous Na2CO3 (1 M, 2.0
eq.) solution were added to a solution of 2- formylphenyl boronic acid
(450 mg, 3.0 mmol) and allyl bromide (1.2 eq.) in THF (0.2 M) The
reaction mixture was heated to reflux and stirred for 4 hours. The
reaction was quenched with H2O and extracted with DCM (x3). The combined
organic layers were washed with brine, dried over MgSO4, and the solvent
removed under reduced pressure. The crude material was purified by column
chromatography (eluent: 95:5 petrol:EtOAc), The title compound in 83%
yield (364 mg, 2.49 mmol). Rf (95:5 Petrol:EtOAc) = 0.49; 1H NMR (300
MHz, CDCl3) δH: 10.24 (1H, s, CHO), 7.84 (1H, dd, J = 7.6, 1.3 Hz, ArH),
7.5 (1H, td, J = 7.4, 1.4 Hz, ArH), 7.39 (1H, td, J = 7.5, 1.0 Hz, ArH),
7.29 (1H, d, J = 7.5 Hz, ArH), 6.03 (1H, ddt, J = 16.9, 10.2, 6.1 Hz,
CHCH2), 5.08 (1H, dq, 10.1, 1.4 Hz, CH=CHAH B ), 4.98 (1H, dq, J = 17.0,
1.6 Hz, CH=CHAH B ), 3.82 (2H, d, J = 6.1 Hz, CH2CH=CH2); 13C{1H} NMR
(75.5 MHz CDCl3) δC: 192.4, 142.3, 137.0, 134.1, 134.0, 132.7, 131.2,
127.0, 116.5, 36.6; I.R (thinfilm) ν max (cm-1): 1692 (C=O), 1598 (C=C),
752 (C=C); HRMS (ESI): m/z calculated for C10H10O: requires: 167.1752 for
[M+Na]+; found: 167.1797.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
