$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM A solution of 2,4-dichloropyrimidine (2.00 g, 13.42 mmol),
4-(4,4,5,5-tetramethyl-1,3,2-dioxaborolan-2-yl)phenol (1.48 g, 6.71
mmol), 2N Na2CO3 (10.07 mL, 20.13 mmol) and Pd(dppf)Cl2 .CH2Cl2 (1.64 g,
2.01 mmol) in toluene/EtOH (v/v = 9/1, 160 mL) was heated to 50°C for 3 h
and monitored by TLC. After cooling to room temperature, the mixture was
poured into water (300 mL), and extracted with EtOAc (500 mL x 2). The
combined organic phases were dried over anhydrous MgSO4,filtered and
concentrated in vacuo. After removal of the solvent, the residue was
purified by flash chromatography (ethylacetate/n-hexane) on silica gel,
4-(2-chloropyrimidin-4-yl)phenol (1.08 g, 78% yield).
